// The skill tree. Each major node is ringed by 8 minor nodes; a point spent on a major opens
// its ring. Every edge has a weight: the points it costs to take the node at its end.
// Taking a minor closes the two next to it in the ring, so at most four of the eight can be had.
//
//   majors: name, title, pos (map units), cost of the ring edges are on each minor,
//           gives: what taking it grants
//   links:  (from, to, weight) between majors; a major can be taken once a linked one is
//   root:   the major every character can take first (costs 1)
//
// Gives: Carry(kg), Air(share of thin air made up), Cold(°C of cold shrugged off),
//        Speed(+share), Mining(+share), Damage(+share), Focus(max), FocusRegen(per s),
//        Spell(Levitation | Light | Warmth), LevitateCost(-share of focus drain)
(
    root: "wanderer",
    majors: [
        (
            name: "wanderer", title: "Wanderer", pos: (0.0, 0.0),
            gives: [Carry(4.0)],
            ring: [
                (title: "Long Stride", cost: 1, gives: [Speed(0.05)]),
                (title: "Pack Mule", cost: 1, gives: [Carry(6.0)]),
                (title: "Deep Lungs", cost: 1, gives: [Air(0.15)]),
                (title: "Thick Skin", cost: 1, gives: [Cold(3.0)]),
